            <ArticleTitle>Management of lithiasis in pelvic kidney through laparoscopy-guided percutaneous transperitoneal nephrolithotripsy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>32-3; discussion 34</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the case of a patient with pain and an abdominal palpable mass whose tests showed a left pelvic kidney with a 1.5-cm stone in the renal pelvis. We describe the successful management through videolaparoscopy-guided percutaneous transperitoneal nephrolithotripsy, stressing that this method is a therapeutic option in such cases.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
